testdisk
Usage: testdisk IMAGE_or_DEVICE

Rebuilds a lost or corrupt partition table and its boot sectors. When a disk
"has no partitions" but the data is still there, testdisk scans for the old
structure and can write it back. Interactive, menu-driven.

	testdisk image.img    operate on a ddrescue image (safer than the disk)
	testdisk /dev/sdX     operate on the device directly

Work on a ddrescue image, not the failing disk, whenever you can.

See also: photorec, ddrescue, smartctl
